{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789000603,"nonce":"I0UvGttYCGbc/Ug6u+Gsj/RNxlY=","title":"--mode jit widens a narrow unsigned register as signed","message":"Three engines agree and the whole-module JIT does not:\n\n                      interp   hybrid   AOT   --mode jit\n    UI8  250 + 1         251      251   251        -5\n    UI8  255 + 1           0        0     0         0\n    UI8  200 * 2         144      144   144      -112\n    UI16 65535 + 1         0        0     0         0\n\n-5 is 251 read as a signed byte and -112 is 144; the two zeros agree because\nthey have no high bit set. So the value is narrowed correctly and then widened\nas signed where HUI8 and HUI16 are unsigned.\n\nReproducer (also at scratchpad/ui8/T4.hx):\n\n    class T4 {\n      static function main() {\n        var e:hl.UI8 = 200;\n        var f:hl.UI8 = e * 2;\n        var fi:Int = f;                       // all three routes are wrong\n        Sys.println(\"via Int local = \" + fi);\n        Sys.println(\"via concat    = \" + (f : Int));\n        var gi:Int = (f : Int) + 0;\n        Sys.println(\"via Int add   = \" + gi);\n      }\n    }\n\nWhat is ruled out, so it is not re-checked:\n\n* Not the string concat or the call marshalling -- an explicit `var fi:Int = f`\n  is wrong on its own.\n* Not `Opcode::ToInt`'s own logic. The AIR dump shows op 5 is\n  `ToInt { dst: Reg(0), src: Reg(3) }`, and that lowering already tests\n  `src_kind == HUI8 || HUI16` and calls `build_int_z_extend`.\n* Not a register-store width mismatch. `ASH_CHECK_REG_STORES=1` reports\n  nothing on this program, and making `UnsafeCast` convert to the destination\n  width changed neither the audit nor the answer.\n\nSo the next place to look is what `reg_types` gives a HUI8 register on this path\nand whether `src_unsigned` is reached at all -- if the slot is already i32 the\nwidth test `sw \u003c dw` is false and the zext never happens, which fits every\nobservation. Note the store audit runs only from `air_emit`, so the\nwhole-module path has no coverage for this class either.","files":null}]}